@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+---
+id: task-002-implement-json-patch-rfc-6902-applypatch
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Patch (RFC 6902) applyPatch"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Second feature of `json-toolkit`: a shared way for services to change JSON documents with standard
+patches, per RFC 6902 (JSON Patch), built on top of `resolvePointer` (RFC 6901, task-001).
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added `applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, along with the
+  `JsonPatchOperation` union type used for its signature (the six RFC 6902 operations: `add`,
+  `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`).
+- `applyPatch` validates that `patch` is an array and that each operation is well-formed (an
+  object with a string `path`, the `value` member required by `add`/`replace`/`test`, the string
+  `from` member required by `move`/`copy`, and a recognised `op`) before applying anything; extra
+  members on an operation are ignored, per RFC 6902 section 4's note.
+- Does not mutate its input: the document is deep-cloned once up front
+  (`deepClone`), and every operation mutates that private clone in place, reassigning it only when
+  an operation targets the whole document (`path: ""`, for `add`/`replace`).
+- Each operation is its own small function (`applyAdd`, `applyRemove`, `applyReplace`,
+  `applyMove`, `applyCopy`, `applyTest`), reusing `resolvePointer` to validate that a target or
+  source location exists where the RFC requires it, and a new `navigateToParent` helper (built on
+  the existing private `step`) to reach the container a pointer's last token refers to for
+  operations that must create that last token (`add`).
+  - `move` is implemented as `remove` from `from` followed by `add` at `path` of the removed
+    value, per RFC 6902 section 4.4; this also means moving a location into its own descendant
+    fails naturally, because the `add` can no longer find its already-removed parent.
+  - `copy` is `add` of a clone of the value at `from`, so the copy never shares structure with its
+    source (see decision-log below).
+  - `test` compares values with a new `deepEqual` (arrays: same length and order; objects: same
+    members regardless of order; everything else: strict equality), per RFC 6902 section 4.6.
+- Tests (`src/index.test.ts`, 26 new cases, all new behaviour so classified red-first; confirmed
+  red — `applyPatch` did not exist — before implementing): covers every RFC 6902 appendix A worked
+  example that applies cleanly to this signature (A.1–A.2, A.3–A.12, A.14–A.16), plus `copy`
+  (including non-aliasing), whole-document `replace`, non-mutation of the input, multi-operation
+  patches, and one error-path test per validation/failure mode not already covered by an appendix
+  example (unknown `op`, missing `value`/`from`, removing the whole document, missing target).
+- Documented the feature in `README.md` with a usage example, next to `resolvePointer`.
+- Verified `src/index.ts` compiles cleanly under the project's strict `tsconfig.json`, using the
+  same temporary, uncommitted `typescript` install approach as task-001; the only typecheck errors
+  are the pre-existing `src/index.test.ts` gap already recorded in dl-001, unchanged by this task.
